#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/id #uuid "021d25c6-08db-5f20-a89b-110389d08e29" :question/math-academy-id "e-3224" :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](images/79/79111226781bc9d3ea9c00e217b93b9661d1e70bdfbee688c555dd899cf3d80e.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-1,1)$ and the radius of the circle is $r = 3.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048811}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561524 :question-generator/id #uuid "a51c1b6b-4fee-5de4-aacf-723e2873fbb4" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087655.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820b9446-f775-5a58-99f1-aaf9f71a8103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085885} {:answer/id #uuid "c318a1b1-16d8-524f-aee8-c1ea71c3ebc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085886} {:answer/id #uuid "068143a